{"agent":"i2-kilo","data":{"budget":"","claim":"A feature item that introduces a new knob/event/command is only given the globs it names, so enforce.commit_without_lease refuses the first write to the shared wiring files (config section + default table, event template, command/parser/api/MCP-tool surfaces); a declarative map keyed by feature class, applied in the single add_task choke point, expands the item's globs before the event is written.","falsifier":"A task declaring adds=[knob] that lands WITHOUT config_sections/*.py and templates/default.toml in its globs refutes it (the wiring globs are absent).","item":"B-item-globs-omit-wiring-files","mechanism":"services.wiring.WIRING maps knob/event/command to their wiring globs; services.items.add_task appends those globs to the draft's (used to write both the task.added event and the lease) when the draft declares .","probe":"uv run pytest -q tests/test_task_add_wiring_globs.py tests/test_item_create.py -p no:cacheprovider","probe_output":"34 passed in 6.05s","question":"Does task add under-declare the wiring files a new command/knob/event must touch, and can services.items.add_task expand them from a declarative map?","sources":[],"verdict":"CONFIRMED"},"id":"e1921e67d05309867561d091d","kind":"research.recorded","lamport":174177,"schema":1,"subject":"R5400d51f2d","ts":"2026-11-11T13:08:51.404764Z"}
